    "user_text": "I remain quiet for a moment, giving Calyx the space I promised.",
    "storyteller_text": "Kessa does not fill the quiet for you.\n\nThe kettle reaches its boil and clicks itself down. Steam clouds the dispatch-box glass, briefly whitening out the freight floor below; when it clears, a lift is rising through the rain with its cage empty and lit from within like a small exposed rib.\n\nThe dead-book sheet remains between you. Your old review notation sits beneath Nera Voss\u2019s name in the Guild\u2019s copied hand: not an accusation broadened for effect, not a charge pretending you opened the shutter yourself. A line in a chain. Enough of one.\n\nKessa takes her cup in both hands and waits.\n\nHer wrist slate gives one soft vibration against the tabletop. She glances down, and something in her face closes before she turns it away. The screen has shown only a sender marker and no message you can read: **I. Senn \u2014 welfare check.**\n\n\u201cHe knows enough to worry,\u201d she says. \u201cThat doesn\u2019t make this his conversation.\u201d\n\nShe moves the slate facedown.\n\nOutside, rain combs the freight lanes flat. The last-rotation board above the door sheds one route after another, amber letters winking out as crews take their loads. Kessa picks up the pen from beside the dead-book page, considers it, and sets it nearer your hand without pressing it into your palm.\n\n\u201cYou can sit here until the kettle goes cold,\u201d she says. \u201cYou can write the sentence. You can refuse it. But don\u2019t mistake quiet for the Guild forgetting why it called you.\u201d\n\nHer eyes rest on the narrow receipt beside the sheet.\n\n\u201cIf you write, you get the fact we have. If you don\u2019t, Tam\u2019s people still have their own night. Don\u2019t use Nera to buy standing with them.\u201d\n\nThe pen lies parallel to the line reserved for your hand. Beyond the glass, a freight cage seals with a heavy, final clack.",
