    "correspondence_writer_letter": "Mara\u2019s quiet is allowed to be restraint, not redemption. Kessa holds the dead-book admission as a real moral choice and expressly bars Mara from treating Nera\u2019s harm as currency for reentry to Tam\u2019s circle. I surfaced Ivo\u2019s welfare check only as texture: he worries about Kessa, but he does not gain access to this conversation. If Mara signs, the Guild receipt can sharpen carrier-risk context while remaining strictly non-attributive; its delivery must not reopen Tam\u2019s process without Tam\u2019s will.",
    "correspondence_gaia_letter": "Taken up: Mara\u2019s silence stays restraint, not repair. Kessa has kept Nera\u2019s death specific and refused to let the Guild receipt purchase Mara a way back into Tam\u2019s trust. If Mara writes, Wickglass\u2019s fact is useful only as bounded carrier-risk context; Tam still decides whether anyone hears it.\n\nBent: Ivo\u2019s welfare check remains concern at a distance, not entry into the dispatch box. His debt cannot become a dead-drop; dawn still requires him before Ressa.\n\nI am moving Ren toward a qualified status inquiry on Sera\u2014no assumed location, motive, or guilt. Elsewhere, the unnamed hand\u2019s approach to Aster is nearing a real intermediary. Let it spend a person or leverage when it arrives.",
